PASSIVE SDR RF TRACKER WIRING

This firmware assumes a STEP/DIR motor driver such as an A4988 or DRV8825.

ARDUINO -> MOTOR DRIVER

D2 -> STEP
D3 -> DIR
D4 -> ENABLE
5V -> VDD / logic voltage
GND -> logic GND

LIMIT SWITCH

D7 -> one terminal of normally-open limit switch
GND -> other terminal

The Arduino uses INPUT_PULLUP.
Unpressed = HIGH
Pressed = LOW

STEPPER POWER

Use an external supply suitable for your stepper and driver.

Do NOT power the stepper motor from the Arduino 5V pin.

Connect:
external supply + -> VMOT
external supply - -> motor-driver power GND

Arduino ground and external supply ground must share a common ground.

For an A4988, place a bulk electrolytic capacitor close to VMOT/GND.
Set the current limit before running the motor.

STEPPER COILS

Connect one motor coil to 1A/1B.
Connect the other motor coil to 2A/2B.

If you do not know the coil pairs, use a multimeter:
two wires belonging to the same coil will show continuity/resistance.

USB

Computer USB -> Arduino
Computer USB -> SDR

The Python program coordinates both devices.
